IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `oapa-nouns`
IMPORT `oapa-threats`

-- Offences against the Person Act 1861 -- TESTS for oapa-threats.l4 (section 16).

§ `Tests: threats to kill`

-- Columns of `Conduct under section 16`:
--   made a threat, had a lawful excuse, intended the other to fear it would be carried
--   out, threat to kill the other person, threat to kill a third person, meant to carry it out
`s16 threat to kill the other, intending fear` MEANS `Conduct under section 16` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s16 threat to kill a third person, intending fear` MEANS `Conduct under section 16` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`s16 lawful excuse` MEANS `Conduct under section 16` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s16 no intention of fear` MEANS `Conduct under section 16` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s16 meant to carry it out but did not intend fear` MEANS `Conduct under section 16` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`s16 intended fear, never meant to carry it out` MEANS `Conduct under section 16` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s16 intended fear, did mean to carry it out` MEANS `Conduct under section 16` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`s16 threat to do something other than kill` MEANS `Conduct under section 16` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s16 no threat made` MEANS `Conduct under section 16` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE

#ASSERT `s 16: threats to kill` `s16 threat to kill the other, intending fear`
#ASSERT `s 16: threats to kill` `s16 threat to kill a third person, intending fear`
-- "without lawful excuse": a lawful excuse takes the case out of the section.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 16: threats to kill` `s16 lawful excuse`)
-- The intention required is that the other would FEAR it would be carried out.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 16: threats to kill` `s16 no intention of fear`)
-- Meaning to carry the threat out is not enough without the intention as to fear.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 16: threats to kill` `s16 meant to carry it out but did not intend fear`)
-- ... and, with the intention as to fear, it makes no difference whether the person
-- meant to carry it out.
#ASSERT `s 16: threats to kill` `s16 intended fear, never meant to carry it out`
#ASSERT `s 16: threats to kill` `s16 intended fear, did mean to carry it out`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 16: threats to kill` `s16 threat to do something other than kill`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 16: threats to kill` `s16 no threat made`)
#ASSERT `s 16: what the text calls the offence` EQUALS `an offence, with no further classification`
#ASSERT `s 16: how the text says the offence is tried` EQUALS `on indictment`
-- ten years = 120 months
#ASSERT `s 16: the sentences the text states` EQUALS LIST `imprisonment` (`for a term not exceeding` 120)
